course: dictionary
lesson: 15751
title: Trike
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A trike is a bike with three wheels, not two. The word is informal, which means people use it in everyday talk, and it is short for tricycle. «Mia rode her red trike round the park.» Mia is riding a bike with three wheels, so a trike must be a three-wheeled ride.
explain: Toddlers ride trikes because three wheels keep them steady. «Tom counted the wheels: the trike had 3.» The wheel count is a clue you can use to check your meaning.
explain: Trike can also mean a motorbike with three wheels. The clues in the sentence tell you which one is meant: pedals and a small child mean a bike, while a loud engine on the road means a motorbike. The phrase «ride a trike» works for both.
fact: A trike is a vehicle with three wheels.
fact: Trike is an informal word for a tricycle.
fact: A trike can mean a small pedal bike for young children, or a motorbike with three wheels.
fact: In wheel-counting maths, one trike has 3 wheels, so two trikes have 6 wheels.
fact: The word tricycle has tri, which means three, and cycle, which means wheel.
exercise: «Mia rode her red trike round the park.» What is a trike? | A bike with two wheels | * A bike with three wheels | A car with four doors | A boat with a sail
exercise: How many wheels does one trike have? | 6 | 2 | 4 | * 3
exercise: Tom says «ride a trike». What might he be doing? | * Riding a three-wheeled bike or motorbike | Sailing a boat across a lake | Flying a kite | Swimming in the sea
test: Two trikes are parked outside the school. How many wheels are there in total? | 9 | 3 | * 6 | 5
test: What does tri mean in the word tricycle? | * Three | Four | One | Two
exam: Which clue shows that trike means a motorbike? | Toddlers laughing in the park | * A loud engine roaring down the road | A basket on the front | Pedals on the seat
